  "title": "“I Gave Birth” Wristbands: A New Approach to Improving Postpartum Safety and Maternal Health",
  "summary": "Hospitals are using “I Gave Birth” postpartum wristbands to remind new mothers and healthcare workers about warning signs and the importance of timely postpartum care. Hospitals in several parts of the United States are turning to a simple silicone wristband as one way to improve postpartum care and help identify potentially serious health complications after childbirth. The “I Gave Birth” wristband initiative was developed to remind new mothers, families, emergency responders and healthcare p",
